      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The Statement bounds the “total number of configurations of M on those inputs” for all inputs of a fixed length n. Take a fixed one-tape machine that reads its first cell and immediately accepts, with s(n)=1. Every branch visits one cell, but its initial configurations over x in {0,1}^n are 2^n distinct because the tape convention defines the initial tape t_x using all symbols of x. This contradicts a bound 2^{c_M} for fixed c_M. Step 1.1 counts only visited portions and thereby omits these differing unvisited input contents.",
